WEBVTT

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.470
I'm home.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.280
Welcome back!

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:14.060
Thick Pudding

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:14.070
Here. Pudding.

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:16.700
Pudding, pudding!

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:18.910
Here, spoo—

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:21.710
<i>How did she eat that?</i>

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.420
What's this?

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.370
It fell from the sky.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.090
What're you talking about?

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:29.670
Oh, I remember this!

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.880
The Light-Up Lie Detector!

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:34.420
Light...?

00:00:35.030 --> 00:00:35.760
What?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.220
The Light-Up Lie Detector.

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.390
Hold it up in front of your eye.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:49.350
I hate pudding.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:55.910
What was that?

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.580
You saw a black, cloudy effect, right?

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:01.830
Yeah.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.270
When that shows up,
 it proves someone's lying to you.

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:08.240
Wait, how do you know that?

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.500
Because this is...

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.270
Part of Nanana's Collection.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.590
I think its official name was
 "The Eye of Yuguthos."

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.730
I found it in ruins, deep in the jungle.

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.260
Y-Yeah?

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:23.460
<i>So they really exist?</i>

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.970
Nanana-chan, what exactly are you?

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:29.690
Just a ghost bound to your room.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:33.750
Still, it's amazing that you 
just happened to find this.

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.440
What exactly are <i>you</i>, Juugo?

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:38.850
Uh... I'm just a high school student.

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:11.960
Why don't you have it?!

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.660
C'mon, Yukihime. Believe it or not,
 I looked all over for it.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:16.740
<b><u>Episode 2:</u></b>

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:16.740
The Nanae Island Third High School Adventure Club

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.920
This is why you're called Hobo-matsu!

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.140
You call me that all the time, 
but my name is Todomatsu.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.460
After all the trouble we 
went through to break in...

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:30.870
After I put a parachute on the
 stolen jewel's case, just as planned,

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.350
and dropped it in the alley!

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:36.480
I guess someone who
 happened to pass through there took it.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:38.980
Is that kind of coincidence even possible?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:42.930
Whatever it takes,
 we'll find who took that jewel,

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:44.740
and as soon as we get it back,

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:46.700
I'll tear them apart.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:56.060
There you are!

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:01.490
Jeez! Why are you
 lying on a pile of garbage?

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.410
Did you do this yourself?

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.300
Why, you ask?

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.430
Because all of the
 answers are here, that's why.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.190
What? You know who stole the jewel?

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:18.470
When the phantom thief troupe, 
Matsuri, passed by overhead,

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:21.650
they put a parachute on the
 jewel and dropped it in this alley.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:25.290
And this is probably a beacon device.

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:27.120
It was in the dumpster.

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:31.080
After that, one of their buddies 
just needed to sneak in and take it.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.040
But it looks like their plan failed.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:39.010
He looked all over the 
place for the target item,

00:04:39.010 --> 00:04:41.240
but I guess he couldn't find it.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:43.350
I see...

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:44.960
You're good!

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:49.430
Now, the question is, who took it?

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:50.680
Yeah.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:54.390
If someone walked through here, 
it must've been coincidence.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.100
Why would they walk 
here that late at night?

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:58.380
The answer is...

00:04:59.050 --> 00:04:59.860
There!

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.320
Welcome.

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.550
<b>Yama Juugo</b>

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.690
Yes?

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:19.670
Oh, good. You're home.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:22.800
A m-maid?! Can I help you?

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.550
From that reaction,
 I guess you really are into maids.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:30.920
You stink!

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:34.460
See? I told you we both should've changed.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.310
Hm. You're right. I do stink.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:39.560
Okay, then let me use your bath, you thief,

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:41.250
Yama Juugo.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.820
Thief? What?

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.930
H-Hey!

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:54.870
Hang on a second! Who are you guys?!

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.830
Oh, just a humble master 
detective and her assistant.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.540
Master detective?

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.990
Master Detective Ikkyuu Tensai!

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:05.140
That's what everyone calls me!

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:07.260
I'm her assistant, Hoshino Daruku.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:18.250
Come to think of it, Nanana-chan, 
you don't have any smell at all.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.940
Um, you said your name is Ikkyuu-san?

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:25.570
Call me by my given name, or my full name.

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:28.750
My surname alone makes 
me sound like some punk.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:33.600
Then, Tensai-san... what brings you here?

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.410
I came to get that back, thief.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.920
Why am I a thief, exactly?

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.380
I have undeniable proof right here!

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.300
That's you, isn't it?

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.800
<b>Video 1</b>

00:06:54.750 --> 00:06:56.820
So that's what you're into, Juugo?

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.700
No, no! It was a total coincidence!

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.600
I mean, you know,
 guys are drawn to that sort of thing...

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:06.440
The mag I <i>just happened</i> to 
pick up had a maid on the cover...

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.150
Subdue him, Daruku!

00:07:10.370 --> 00:07:12.740
Whoa! Uh, Miss Maid,
 this is very bold of you...

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:14.450
I mean, no! Don't look!

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.420
What are you doing?!

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.170
What the hell?!

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.560
By the way, Daruku is not a boy.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:31.120
<b>Boy</b>

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:31.130
He's a trap.

00:07:29.690 --> 00:07:31.120
<b>Trap</b>

00:07:32.630 --> 00:07:34.350
Now, this is the scene in question!

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:45.090
Juugo, you slimeball.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:46.270
Wait a minute!

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.790
My phone started buzzing in my pocket,
 so I was just surprised!

00:07:49.790 --> 00:07:54.720
Daruku, as a male, what do you think 
happened to this thief in that moment?

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:59.860
Um, I think... h-he got aroused and...
 well... his position...

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:02.210
Hey, fake maid!
 Why are you squirming like that?!

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.870
A-Anyway, I'm innocent!

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.540
So the thief says.

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.260
But there is no record of a received call,

00:08:07.830 --> 00:08:12.010
<b>No messages</b>

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:12.010
or even an email,
 on your phone from that time.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.760
Don't check my phone without permission!

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.810
I won't be talking to you for a while.

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.700
Now all the mysteries are solved.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.640
Hang on! Nothing's solved at all!

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.850
You haven't explained anything here!

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.910
I'm saying, it was two 
minutes after this scene

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:30.190
when the jewel thief passed
 over a building close to this one.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.420
The only customer at the convenience
 store during that time was you, thief.

00:08:34.420 --> 00:08:36.580
From your clothes, I knew you were a local.

00:08:36.580 --> 00:08:38.880
It was already past the school dorm's curfew,

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:41.120
so I began searching 
 all nearby apartments.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.660
No, that doesn't tell me anything!

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:48.530
I'm pretty sure Tensai has all the theories 
worked out and solved it in her own head,

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:51.290
but she's just not very good 
at explaining things to others.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:53.010
I'm telling you, that's the problem!

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.060
Well, I did think...

00:08:57.750 --> 00:09:01.350
It was pretty amazing that you 
figured out it was me who found it.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.550
Indeed. You are a good man, thief.

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:07.470
By the way, I didn't get your name yet.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:09.670
Tell me, Yama Juugo.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:13.400
Uh, you just said it yourself.
 Yama Juugo.

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.930
No, I mean, what's your real name?

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:19.580
I'm telling you, my real name is Yama Juugo!

00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:23.780
Is that so? All right, got it.
 I'll remember that.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.080
And what's your girlfriend's name?

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:30.100
Me? I'm Ryuugajou Nanana.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:31.900
Oh, and I'm not his girlfriend.

00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:35.040
I'm a total stranger with no 
connection to Juugo whatsoever.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:37.890
What's your real name?

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.720
Uh, it's Ryuugajou Nanana.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.180
I see. I'll remember that.

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:50.370
I'll take responsibility for delivering 
this stolen jewel to the police.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:51.480
Rest at ease.

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:59.160
<b>Good Morning,</b>

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:59.160
<b>Nanae Island</b>

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.480
<i>Last night, just before dawn,</i>

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:04.370
<b><i>Headline News</i></b>

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:04.370
<b>Thief turns self in, carrying stolen goods</b>

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:02.260
<i>the Seven's Building robbery culprit</i>

00:10:02.260 --> 00:10:04.370
<i>surrendered to police, 
with the stolen goods.</i>

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:07.460
<i>The underaged girl charged with the</i>

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:12.090
<i>theft repeatedly made nonsensical statements 
such as, "I'm a master detective."</i>

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:16.630
<b><i>Headline News</i></b>

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:16.630
<b>Thief turns self in, carrying stolen goods</b>

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:14.770
<i>Her motive is now under investigation.</i>

00:10:15.390 --> 00:10:16.590
<i>Next in the news...</i>

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.620
So long, master detective.

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:22.110
I doubt we'll ever meet again.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:26.230
Well, uh... I'm going now.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:34.900
I'm Hoshino Daruku.

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.910
I'm Master Detective Ikkyuu Tensai.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:45.680
"Master Detective"? What the heck?!

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:47.560
What is she talking about?!

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:55.290
Well, what a happy coincidence, Juugo.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:57.010
I didn't particularly want to see you.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:02.100
And why aren't you mad after 
they laughed at you like that?

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:04.310
Why should I care if they laugh at me?

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:07.730
This is what the people 
who laughed are thinking:

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:13.980
"What madness is that cute 
transfer student talking about?"

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:16.730
Well, I can agree with that,
 except the "cute" part.

00:11:17.210 --> 00:11:21.710
It's true that I am not yet a master 
detective in the true sense of the term.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:25.620
That's why people laugh, 
and why I make you worry.

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.370
I wasn't worried about you.

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:31.540
But what if I were to

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:34.340
become a genuine master detective 
in both name and deed?

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:38.010
They would be surprised and
 feel the shame of their mistake.

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:41.970
Once that happens, I've won!

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:48.140
Is Yama Juugo-san here?

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:58.690
Miss Maid, what can I do for you?

00:11:59.140 --> 00:12:02.660
May I have a moment of 
your time, Yama Juugo-san?

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:07.120
Of course! If a maid 
in glasses wishes it...

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:10.830
Pleased to meet you, Yama Juugo-kun.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:15.460
I'm Yuiga Isshin, a third-year student.

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:17.690
I'm the president of this club.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:20.110
Thank you for coming today.

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:23.540
You're the one who called me?

00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:25.180
Yes, that's right.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.030
I'm going now.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:32.110
Why do you think you can leave, scum?

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:36.230
Listen to Isshin-sama, you dumbass!

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.650
Ow! Ow! Please stop!

00:12:39.090 --> 00:12:40.670
Juugo-kun!

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:41.540
I've been fooled by a maid yet again!

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:42.650
Juugo-san...

00:12:41.540 --> 00:12:42.650
Damn it!

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.150
Stop, Yuu.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:48.660
Yes, Isshin-sama.

00:12:49.560 --> 00:12:52.970
She's a third-year student and
 our vice president, Ibara Yuu.

00:12:52.970 --> 00:12:55.150
I looked into you a bit,

00:12:55.150 --> 00:12:58.490
and found out that you like 
maids and girls with glasses.

00:12:58.920 --> 00:13:00.550
What do you want from me?

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:04.680
I would like to welcome 
you to the Adventure Club.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.390
<i>Adventure Club?</i>

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.390
<b>...interested, see the Adventure Club at...</b>

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.350
Um... what's the club after?

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:13.100
Nanana's Collection.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:20.190
Yama-kun, would you mind if I 
paid a visit to your apartment?

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:24.780
It's good to see you again, Nanana-san.

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:27.370
It's been a long time, Yuiga-kun.

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:28.650
A whole year!

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:30.410
What brings you here today?

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:35.980
Actually, I'm scouting 
Yama-kun for the Adventure Club.

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:39.000
Beginning with Konjou-senpai, 
the one who founded the club,

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:43.830
all those who live in this apartment 
are essential to the Adventure Club.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:43.130
<b>Konjou Kasumi</b>

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:45.330
Hmm, I see...

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:47.380
<i>Konjou... from the Nanana Manual?</i>

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:49.760
This is a mere token of our esteem,
 but please accept it.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:51.570
Yay!

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.030
It's Randoya Light Pudding!

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:57.350
Thanks, Yuiga-kun!

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:00.490
I'm glad you seem pleased with it.

00:14:00.490 --> 00:14:04.260
Then, I'll be taking my leave for today.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:07.890
What? You're leaving already?

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:08.530
Yes.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:13.170
I'm sure I'll be depending 
on you again in the future.

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.290
Please give me your guidance then.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:20.210
Should you ever feel up to it,
 come visit anytime.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:25.640
Pudding, pudding!

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.970
Randoya!

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:36.180
It's so good, I'm gonna die!

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:39.140
<i>Whew, good.
 Looks like she's in a better mood.</i>

00:14:39.560 --> 00:14:42.020
Hey, are you gonna join the Adventure Club?

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:45.150
I don't mind joining,
 but I don't have any reason to.

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:48.880
You're not into Nanana's Collection?

00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:50.740
Actually, I want to ask you...

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:55.590
You're really not mad about people
 taking the treasures you collected?

00:14:56.660 --> 00:15:00.030
I loved treasure hunting, too.

00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.660
I'd rather see people find them.

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:04.070
You're one weird ghost.

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:05.210
I'm not weird!

00:15:05.910 --> 00:15:08.740
I know that's the right thing.

00:15:08.740 --> 00:15:13.140
Happiness is only happiness 
when everyone shares it.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:18.490
Nanana-chan, do you want to move on?

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:20.310
Where's this coming from?

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:26.480
I love online games, so I don't 
want to move on for a while yet...

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:29.450
But I want to find whoever killed me.

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:31.980
That won't be easy to do now, though.

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:33.320
A dragon mark.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:33.910
Huh?

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:38.300
The killer had a dragon
 mark on the back of their neck.

00:15:38.650 --> 00:15:40.620
How do you have an
 incredible clue like that?!

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.920
Even with it, no one's found the killer.

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:46.380
You'll really help me find who did it?

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:49.340
Well, if I feel like it.

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:53.550
Is it because you want me to go away?

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:57.610
That's not it... I mean...

00:15:58.070 --> 00:16:01.770
I guess I'm kind of
 interested in you, in some way...

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:04.410
Really?

00:16:04.410 --> 00:16:07.140
Then try to find Nanana's Collection.

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:10.660
You might find something that'll 
help you track down the killer.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:11.740
Oh, yeah...

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:15.590
Then tell me where
 Nanana's Collection is hidden.

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:18.790
Huh? I obviously can't do that.

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.530
Obviously?

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:22.460
But why? It's for your own sake!

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:25.670
So you are doing it for me? I'm glad.

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.380
I didn't mean that!

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:30.680
Why won't you tell me?

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:32.050
Tell me the reason, please!

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:34.750
Because that wouldn't be any fun!

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:39.060
An entry test?

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.280
It's a tradition within our club.

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:43.770
You must clear this test to join.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:45.610
All right, then.

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:48.230
And? Why are you two here?

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:50.730
It seemed like fun, so I followed you.

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:55.200
Tensai followed you, so I did, too.

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.570
Don't follow me around...

00:16:57.940 --> 00:17:01.620
All right. The three of
 you will take the test, then.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:05.750
There's a room in this school that once
 held a Nanana's Collection treasure.

00:17:06.980 --> 00:17:09.210
It doesn't matter how much you fail.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.670
All you need to do is conquer that room.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:13.170
No Entry

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.550
No Entry

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.800
Off you go!

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:18.390
What, you're not coming?!

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.650
I'll be watching you, for now.

00:17:20.650 --> 00:17:22.350
And I'm... observing.

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:25.310
Oh, is that right? Have it your way.

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:06.520
I don't really get all this,
 but I need to open that box, right?

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:16.070
You're kidding me!

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:22.100
Hey! You okay?

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.350
Now this is interesting!

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.290
That was nothi—

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.600
Juugo-kun is really something.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.820
That was the tenth time.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:48.810
But he knows how to take a 
fall without hurting himself.

00:18:52.180 --> 00:18:54.780
You're right. He's only scratched.

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:57.860
And he has the stamina to 
keep running and running.

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:00.320
Looks like he's built himself up well.

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:06.540
Well, I guess it's time I went in, too.

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.360
I'll have a go at it next.

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:11.250
What?!

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:22.090
Hm...

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:28.610
Tensai, there's a treasure chest.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:31.510
Indeed. Let's search the area first.

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:34.060
Hey, wait!

00:19:34.060 --> 00:19:35.270
It's dangerous!

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:38.030
Tensai!

00:19:38.980 --> 00:19:41.270
You think he's okay?

00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:42.990
That's kinda painful, you know.

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:46.700
Yes. I understand this setup.

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:46.700
Ignoring me?!
 You're a real piece of work...

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:53.880
Don't Forget Anything

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:00.320
Juugo, what is today, again?

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:02.170
Huh? It's Thursday.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:03.260
Then...

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:06.390
We do this.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:07.140
<b>Philosophy for Everyone</b>

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:07.850
<b>Japanese Made Fun</b>

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.310
<b>Math 1</b>

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.740
It doesn't reach to the end...

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:22.280
But that's all of them, isn't it?

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:24.320
Oh, right...

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:30.190
I was forgetting my lunch.

00:20:30.730 --> 00:20:32.120
Okay, let's go.

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.130
<b>Mon.  Tue.  Wed.  Thu.  Fri.</b>

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:41.130
<b>Japanese  Japanese  Math  Philosophy  Japanese
Math  PE  Japanese  Japanese  Life Studies
Music  Life Studies  Art  Music  PE
Japanese  Life Studies  Art  Math  Japanese
Homeroom  Math  Writing  English</b>

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:58.440
Wow...

00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:00.980
It's over? That was fast.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:04.240
I can't believe you figured it out
 from  the poster and class schedule.

00:21:04.760 --> 00:21:07.200
There was nothing
 difficult about this at all.

00:21:07.620 --> 00:21:09.330
This is elementary level.

00:21:10.360 --> 00:21:13.290
That getup suits you.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:17.500
Shut up!

00:21:21.160 --> 00:21:24.250
Tensai!
